<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <title>Boundary Validation Demo</title>
  <style>
    body { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 900px; margin: 40px auto; padding: 0 20px; }
    h1 { color: #2c3e50; }
    h2 { color: #3498db; border-bottom: 2px solid #3498db; padding-bottom: 8px; }
    .result { background: #d4edda; border: 1px solid #27ae60; padding: 16px; border-radius: 8px; }
    code { background: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px; }
    a { color: #3498db; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <h1>Boundary Validation Demo</h1>
  <p>This route parses <code>req.query</code> through a zod schema before it reaches any template.
     Untrusted input arrives as <code>unknown</code> and is narrowed to a typed domain value:
     the <code>unknown</code> &rarr; schema-parse &rarr; domain pattern.</p>

  <section class="result">
    <h2>Parsed &amp; validated values</h2>
    <p><strong>name:</strong> {{ name }}</p>
    <p><strong>count:</strong> {{ count }}</p>
  </section>

  <p>Try invalid input:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/boundary?name=Alice&count=5">/boundary?name=Alice&amp;count=5</a> (valid)</li>
    <li><a href="/boundary?name=&count=0">/boundary?name=&amp;count=0</a> (empty name, non-positive count &rarr; 400)</li>
    <li><a href="/boundary?name=Alice">/boundary?name=Alice</a> (missing count &rarr; 400)</li>
  </ul>

  <p><a href="/">Back to Index</a></p>
</body>
</html>
